  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Faithful Desktop",
    "overview": "This portfolio desktop is not styled after Ubuntu; it is Ubuntu 26.04's Yaru look rebuilt in the browser, and the fidelity itself is the portfolio piece. Every surface answers to a GNOME or libadwaita original: the near-black top bar, the translucent left dock, the 46px headerbar with round title buttons, boxed lists, pill quick toggles, the Show Apps grid. Content lives in windows you open, never on a scrolling page.\n\nThe system is two-layered. The **shell** (top bar, dock, app grid, popovers, banners, session screens) floats over a full-bleed wallpaper with dark translucency and large soft radii. The **apps** sit inside windows on flat Yaru neutrals with hairline separators. One colour connects them: the live accent `--brand`, chosen by the visitor from Yaru's ten accents, which recolours wallpaper, suggested actions, toggles, switches, sliders, focus rings, selection and the close button on hover.\n\nDensity is desktop density: 13 to 15px text, 34 to 54px hit targets, 8 to 16px gaps. Light and dark styles are both first-class and swap the whole neutral set, shell included.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Faithful Ubuntu 26.04 / Yaru chrome, light and dark.",
      "One live accent (`--brand`) out of ten Yaru colours; everything else neutral.",
      "Montserrat everywhere; Ubuntu Mono only for terminal output and literal code.",
      "Shell surfaces translucent and dark; app surfaces flat and tonal.",
      "Suru squircle app icons and procedural, accent-painted wallpapers.",
      "Expo-out motion that disappears entirely under reduced motion or Power Saver."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Accent Rule",
        "body": "`--brand` is the only saturated UI colour. Anything that signals \"selected\", \"on\", \"primary\" or \"focused\" uses it; nothing else invents a second accent. Change the accent, and every such state must follow.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Neutral Accent Rule",
        "body": "shadcn's `accent` token is a neutral hover fill, not the brand. Never map `accent` to `--brand`; use `brand` / `primary` for the colour.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Family Rule",
        "body": "Montserrat is the only UI face. Ubuntu Mono appears only where text is literally code or terminal output.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Clock Rule",
        "body": "Clocks, countdowns, battery percent and stats use tabular figures (`.tabular`) so digits never jitter.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Focus Lifts Rule",
        "body": "Only the focused window carries the deep shadow and the full headerbar tone; every other window sinks to the backdrop shadow, backdrop headerbar and dimmed title.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Suru Squircle",
        "body": "App icons are a superellipse (`M24 3c13.3 0 21 4.4 21 21s-7.7 21-21 21S3 37.3 3 24 10.7 3 24 3Z` on a 48 grid) filled with the app's tile colour, a diagonal fold (`M48 10 10 48h38Z` at 13% black), a top highlight gradient, a 12% black outline and a 1px drop shadow, with a solid Heroicons glyph at 52% of the tile.",
        "section": "shapes"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** route every \"on / selected / primary / focused\" state through `--brand` so the accent switch recolours it.",
      "**Do** keep window chrome exact: 46px headerbar, 12px radius, 24px round title buttons, close turning `--brand` on hover.",
      "**Do** build app UI from the `_ui.tsx` libadwaita primitives and portal headerbar content through `HeaderBar`.",
      "**Do** use shell tokens (shell, shell-card, panel, dock) for anything that floats over the desktop, and window tokens for anything inside a window.",
      "**Do** take a z-index from the fixed stacking ladder in Layout.",
      "**Do** honour reduced motion and Power Saver: every new animation must collapse under `.no-anim` and the media query.",
      "**Do** use Heroicons (solid) for app and UI icons, with custom SVG glyphs only where GNOME has no Heroicons equivalent."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** map shadcn's `accent` token to the brand; it is the neutral hover fill.",
      "**Don't** introduce a second saturated UI colour or a font other than Montserrat (Ubuntu Mono is for code only).",
      "**Don't** use raster wallpapers or heavy image assets; wallpapers are procedural SVG painted with the accent.",
      "**Don't** give a window its own drawn headerbar or title buttons; the shell owns window chrome.",
      "**Don't** animate a window with `transform`; use the individual `scale` and `translate` properties so the positioning transform survives."
    ]
  }
}
